 true] [17592186351317 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351319 13194139535479 true] [17592186351317 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351320 13194139535479 true] [17592186351317 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535479 true] [17592186351317 1041 "field-4" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351317 1104 #edb/ref 17592186351320 13194139535479 true] [17592186351317 1110 #uuid "dd110000-e9ff-5a62-83c8-17d5dd053b5a" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351318 1034 "an irregular singular" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351318 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535479 true] [17592186351318 1111 #uuid "420d5257-7ec2-5759-b45f-f9a4d23dc084" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351319 1034 "an ordinary" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351319 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535479 true] [17592186351319 1111 #uuid "eaae1990-82da-5722-9700-50708fadad04" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351320 1034 "a regular singular" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351320 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535479 true] [17592186351320 1111 #uuid "518066db-d9fe-59c1-aa1a-febc5d2439f7" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351321 1017 #edb/ref 17592186351322 13194139535479 true] [17592186351321 1017 #edb/ref 17592186351326 13194139535479 true] [17592186351321 1017 #edb/ref 17592186351330 13194139535479 true] [17592186351321 1017 #edb/ref 17592186351334 13194139535479 true] [17592186351321 1089 "q-342642" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351321 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535479 true] [17592186351321 1100 "$$\nx(x-2)(x+1){y}^{″}+x(x+1){y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}y=0\n$$\n\nClassify the following points for the differential equation given above.$\\,$The point $x=1$ is\n{{field-1}}\npoint of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$The point $x=-1$ is\n{{field-2}}\npoint of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$The point $x=0$ is\n{{field-3}}\npoint of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$The point $x=2$ is\n{{field-4}}\npoint of the differential equation." 13194139535479 true] [17592186351321 1113 #uuid "815bad48-989e-5078-af03-3c8c64dddf2b" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351321 1145 "The point $x=a$ is an ordinary point of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x)\n$$\n\nif both $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, $x=a$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\nA singular point $x=a$ is regular if both $(x-a)P(x)$ and $(x-a)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, the singular point is irregular.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the differential equation in standard form by dividing by $x(x-2)(x+1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(x-2)(x+1){y}^{″}+x(x+1){y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{x-2}{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}(x-2)(x+1)}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}(x-2)(x+1)}.\n$$\n\nThe function $P(x)$ is *not* analytic about points where $x-2=0,$ which occurs at $x=2.$\n\nThe function $Q(x)$ is *not* analytic about points where ${x}^{3}(x-2)(x+1)=0,$ which occurs at $x=0,$ $x=2,$ and $x=-1.$\n\nTherefore, $x=1$ is $\\text{an ordinary}$ point of the differential equation, and the singular points are\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,x=2,\\,x=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's classify each singular point.\n\n- For $x=0,$ the function\n\n$$\nxP(x)=x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x-2},\n$$\n\nis analytic about $x=0,$ while the function\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}Q(x)={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}(x-2)(x+1)}=\\frac{1}{x(x-2)(x+1)},\n$$\n\nis *not* analytic about $x=0.$ Thus, $x=0$ is $\\text{an irregular singular}$ point of the differential equation.\n\n- For $x=2,$ the function\n\n$$\n(x-2)P(x)=(x-2)\\cdot \\frac{1}{x-2}=1,\n$$\n\nis analytic about $x=2,$ and the function\n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}Q(x)=(x-2)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}(x-2)(x+1)}=\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{3}(x+1)},\n$$\n\nis also analytic about $x=2.$ Therefore, $x=2$ is $\\text{a regular singular}$ point of the differential equation.\n\n- For $x=-1,$ the function\n\n$$\n(x+1)P(x)=(x+1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{x-2},\n$$\n\nis analytic about $x=-1,$ and the function\n\n$$\n(x+1)^{2}Q(x)=(x+1)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}(x-2)(x+1)}=\\frac{x+1}{{x}^{3}(x-2)},\n$$\n\nis also analytic about $x=-1.$ Therefore, $x=-1$ is $\\text{a regular singular}$ point of the differential equation." 13194139535479 true] [17592186351322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351323 13194139535479 true] [17592186351322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351324 13194139535479 true] [17592186351322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351325 13194139535479 true] [17592186351322 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535479 true] [17592186351322 1041 "field-1" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351322 1104 #edb/ref 17592186351324 13194139535479 true] [17592186351322 1110 #uuid "cf6df1cb-fde7-53ff-a280-7bb406b01e83" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351323 1034 "an irregular singular" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351323 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535479 true] [17592186351323 1111 #uuid "e96e2cac-87c9-5fe7-9807-c473a3c3dd0c" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351324 1034 "an ordinary" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351324 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535479 true] [17592186351324 1111 #uuid "e9d8c7b4-9a31-5999-8f7a-ed9b6a90a0cb" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351325 1034 "a regular singular" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351325 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535479 true] [17592186351325 1111 #uuid "799bdad1-c5cb-5f3e-a5ca-5c4474c2c822" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351327 13194139535479 true] [17592186351326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351328 13194139535479 true] [17592186351326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351329 13194139535479 true] [17592186351326 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535479 true] [17592186351326 1041 "field-2" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351326 1104 #edb/ref 17592186351329 13194139535479 true] [17592186351326 1110 #uuid "23842176-ddaa-540a-976e-737d69a9d9bd" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351327 1034 "an irregular singular" 13194139535479 true] [17592186351327 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535479 true] [17592186351327 1111 #uuid "052596c0-a9b4-5f02-ae61-662417c6dc91" 13194139535479 true]